        "evidence": "Table only.",
        "notes": "Two structural notes. (1) The stratification is not a partition as tabulated: Lambda_2 appears twice, once for lambda_pair ('Lambda_2 contains (n-2,2), (n-2,1,1)') and once for a_K ('Lambda_2 chirality projection'), while the proof sibling's argument turns on 'every lambda enters exactly one stratum'. Either a_K is a projection WITHIN Lambda_2 rather than a stratum assignment, in which case the column is overloaded, or the partition claim needs weakening. Lambda_3 is likewise given as a 'chirality-cell sub-stratum' and Lambda_{>=4} as a 'universal tail', so three of the seven rows are not plain strata. (2) The lambda_shell prefactor is given as 'm_e * 8 G from gravity prefactor'. G is not defined anywhere in this table or its parent, and if it is the gravitational constant then m_e*8G is not an energy, so the row is dimensionally unreadable as written; the cited prop:gravity-spectral-prefactor presumably fixes the normalisation, but a reader of the table cannot tell."
      }
